--TEST--
a class and an interface redeclaring an inherited constant at another type are refused, `int` over `float` included, since a `static::NAME` read is typed where the constant is declared, `rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
interface Named {
    public const string NAME = "named";
}

interface Titled extends Named {
    public const int NAME = 1;
}

class Base {
    public const string PATH = "/";
}

class Child extends Base {
    public const int PATH = 3;
}

class Fine extends Base {
    public const string PATH = "/fine";
}

class Rate {
    public const float RATE = 1.5;
}

class WholeRate extends Rate {
    public const int RATE = 2;
}

echo "after\n";
// covers: lang:classes/interfaces
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0833]: `Titled::NAME` is `int`, and `Named::NAME` is `string`
  --> case.nvs:7:22
%A
error[E0833]: `Child::PATH` is `int`, and `Base::PATH` is `string`
   --> case.nvs:15:22
%A
error[E0833]: `WholeRate::RATE` is `int`, and `Rate::RATE` is `float`
   --> case.nvs:27:22
%A
